completed: codex (run=RUN-260831-1ce05f, pid=41711, exit=1)\nspawn autonomous recovery: run RUN-260831-1ce05f queued successor RUN-260831-0a4533 (attempt 1/3, model=gpt-5.6-sol): spawned agent exited with code 1\nspawn run started: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (run=RUN-260831-0a4533)\nagent completed: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (exit=0)\nspawn run completed: codex (run=RUN-260831-0a4533, pid=61816, exit=0)\nOrchestrator re-scope after CR revision 3 review. This task began as fuzz coverage and has grown, by successive review findings, into the owner of the scoped Section 10.1-10.4 closed-shape conformance gate. That growth is legitimate: three consecutive reviews proved that identity was attesting structurally invalid objects, and a fuzz task cannot honestly pass while the gate it fuzzes admits what the contract rejects. The scope field is updated to say so rather than leaving the task pretending to be narrower than it is. Splitting the work into a new task was considered and rejected because the validator is already in flight in this candidate. Method requirement for this rework: the previous two rounds each fixed exactly the fields the reviewer named and were then defeated by the next unenumerated field. Do not repeat that. Enumerate every declared constraint in the pinned Sections 10.1-10.4 systematically from SPEC.md, record the enumeration as evidence, and implement against that list. Reviewer finding F2 also stands: README claimed a completed audit that had not happened, so claims must be reproducible through both public entries or removed.\nSTORY-260830-2wdm5e base refresh SKIPPED: the managed workspace holds uncommitted work, so there was no clean checkpoint branch to replay onto trunk e8f8e2febfbc; the branch is unchanged at fork point c9e5290b1506\nspawn workload selection: class=implementation source=derived policy=spawn.workload_classes pair=codex/gpt-5.6-sol/high pair_source=explicit match=recommended_rank_1 snapshot=sha256:f7130ab6b2ae6c4bf7bde632137d1e