run=RUN-260831-baf438, pid=54730, exit=1)\nspawn autonomous recovery: run RUN-260831-baf438 queued successor RUN-260831-273ee2 (attempt 1/3, model=gpt-5.6-sol): spawned agent exited with code 1\nspawn run started: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (run=RUN-260831-273ee2)\nagent completed: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (exit=1)\nspawn run completed: codex (run=RUN-260831-273ee2, pid=63472, exit=1)\nspawn autonomous recovery: run RUN-260831-273ee2 queued successor RUN-260831-60192c (attempt 2/3, model=gpt-5.6-sol): spawned agent exited with code 1\nspawn run started: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (run=RUN-260831-60192c)\nagent completed: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (exit=0)\nspawn run completed: codex (run=RUN-260831-60192c, pid=86097, exit=0)\nFifth review round, and the failure mode is structural rather than substantive. Each round the validator gains cases for exactly the schemas the previous review named, and the next review finds the next uncovered schema. Revision 4 has schema-specific cases only for Blob Descriptor and Transfer Manifest, so every other registered immutable schema including urn:ax:schema:session-record@1.0.0 falls through to extension-only validation and is attested without its Section 10.1 envelope members. Stop enumerating. Make the property total: every schema in the registered self-identity set must resolve to a schema-specific shape validator, and add a completeness test DERIVED FROM THE REGISTRY that fails when any registered schema lacks one. That is the same structural fix that ended the identical cycle on the normative pin task, where a derived union plus a regression assertion replaced a hand-picked list. Where member sets can be read from the pinned specification or the generated contract catalog, derive them rather than transcribing. A schema whose shape genuinely has no additional constraints beyond the envelope still needs an explicit registered validator saying so, not a fall-through.\nspawn workload selection: class=implementation source=derived policy=spawn.workload_classes pair=codex/gpt-5.6-sol/high pair_source=explicit match=recommended_rank_1 snapshot=sha256:f7130ab6b2ae6c4bf7bde632137d1eb646cbd3be7f4039acc56d0cf5f965b005 rationale="Following rank-1 recommendation: four rounds of enumerating named schemas have not converged; the validator must become total over the registry with a derived completeness test."\nspawn agent resolution: Agent selection: codex via explicit_override (preferred_agentic_system: exclusive[codex], config: spawn.preferred_agentic_system)\nspawn launch composition: empty; contract=agents-infra.child-launch-composition; provider=codex; schema=1; producer=v1.6.1; diagnostic=launch_composition_empty; no project MCP servers enabled\nspawn queued: [implementer] developer (codex) (run=RUN-260831-0d504d, max_parallel=20)\nspawn run started: [implementer] developer (codex) (run=RUN-260831-0d504d)\nRevision 6 removes the catalog-recognition attestation bypass with a total explicit schema/version shape-validator registry. Session Record 1.0 is closed recursively; remaining unavailable shapes refuse explicitly. Full configured validation is green; four bounded fuzz targets ran directly. Evidence: TASK-260830-8x76g1_rework-rev6-results.md, TASK-260830-8x76g1_rework-rev6-logbook.md, TASK-260830-8x76g1_rework-rev6-validation-logs.tar.gz. task-board validate exited 0 with 262 inherited MISSING_ACTIVITY diagnostics recorded in evidence.\nagent completed: [implementer] developer (codex) (exit=0)\nspawn run completed: codex (run=RUN-260831-0d504d, pid=11783, exit=0)\nspawn autonomous recovery: run RUN-260831-0d504d queued successor RUN-260831-9abe3a (attempt 1/3, model=gpt-5.6-sol): Change Request construction for TASK-260830-8x76g1 failed: Change Request CR-TASK-260830-8x76g1-5 revision 5 validation failed at command 1/13 (1-based) with exit code 1; log resource TASK-260830-8x76g1_change-request_rev5-validation.log; retry: fix the failure and complete the producer again; the configured suit